title: 'HRMP: New Deposit Flow'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet now takes and gives back channel deposits through a new
    `DepositProvider` trait from `hrmp-primitives`, set as `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`.
    `init_open_channel`, `accept_open_channel` and `poke_channel_deposits` run their checks and
    request the deposit. Storage is written and events are emitted only when the provider reports
    back through `on_deposit_result`, so a provider on another chain can finish the call later.
    Refunds on cancel, close, offboarding and a lowered poke go through `DepositProvider::refund`.

    `LocalDepositProvider` reserves and unreserves through `Config::Currency` and reports success
    in the same call, so existing runtimes behave as before. This is a breaking change for
    `polkadot-runtime-parachains`: every runtime must now set `type DepositProvider`, and
    `LocalDepositProvider<Runtime>` works as a drop-in.
crates:
- name: hrmp-primitives
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
